notes+='\n## Sources.docx alignment\n\nThe supplied HomeCycle SDD is used only as a presentation example: architecture with component explanations; backend, website and field-client package diagrams with No / Package / Description; a domain class diagram followed by separately numbered sequence sections per feature. Class operations and interface names remain proposed design contracts for GrainLedger. No HomeCycle business feature or external integration is adopted. The example contains some duplicate subsection numbers; the revised document uses consecutive numbering.\n'
(ROOT/'design_basis_and_traceability.md').write_text(notes)
s='# IV. Software Design Description\n\n'
s+='GrainLedger — SDD design revision 0.2, 16 October 2026. The presentation follows the SDD example in Sources.docx. Interface names and methods are proposed design contracts; business rules and entity names follow the supplied GrainLedger SRS, use cases and ERD.\n\n'
s+='## 1. System Design\n\n### 1.1 System Architecture\n\n![System Architecture](diagrams/01_system_architecture.svg)\n\nDiagram 1: System Architecture\n\n**Component Explanations**\n\n'
s+='GrainLedger uses a proposed modular backend with separated API, Application, Domain and Infrastructure responsibilities. The field web client and operations website use the same protected application contracts. This arrangement keeps stock, reservation, approval and CLOSE changes within the required transaction boundary.\n\n'
components=[
 ('Presentation Layer (Frontend)','The Operations and Compliance Website serves the six internal roles through scoped workflows. The mobile-friendly Field Web Client captures farmer/plot, declarations, receipt and sample data, retains pending payloads offline and synchronizes on reconnection. It is the web client specified by GrainLedger, rather than the native mobile application used by the example project.'),
 ('API Layer — GrainLedger.API','Controllers obtain the authenticated actor, check request shape and invoke application operations. Shared middleware supplies scope/correlation and maps failures. HTTPS carries commands, queries and reconciliation outcomes. Authorization is enforced on the server for each action and direct object access.'),
 ('Application Layer — GrainLedger.Application','Application services coordinate procurement, physical operations/corrections, stock/reservations, evidence/compliance, order planning/review, loading/CLOSE, trace/HOLD, administration and history. Repository and UnitOfWork interfaces keep all related writes in one protected transaction.'),
 ('Domain Layer — GrainLedger.Domain','Domain objects represent customer-owned lots, mass contributions, evidence versions, plan authority, reservations and shipment state. Policies enforce same-owner use, valid stages, exact decimal arithmetic, signed variance, sufficient evidence and retained decision history.'),
 ('Infrastructure Layer — GrainLedger.Infrastructure','Repositories map logical classes to the supplied physical model, including stock_positions, stock_postings and offline_operations. Persistence adapters provide locking/freshness checks, append-only records and immutable snapshots. Adapter technology remains a project implementation decision.'),
 ('Persistence and Immutable Content','Authoritative ledger postings, reservation events, evidence versions, assessment bases, notices and closing dossiers are persisted durably. Immutable content may use the supplied transactional JSONB/snapshot/hash representation; a separate external storage product is not required. Stock projections are updated only through protected ledger transactions.'),
 ('Build and Deployment','The proposal requires containerized delivery and a CI/CD pipeline. Build, test and package steps deliver the web clients and backend deployment. The sample project hosting vendors, framework versions and CI provider are not requirements for GrainLedger.'),
 ('External Information Sources','Laboratory reports and MRL reference publications are external information sources. Customer Manager registers lab evidence; Mill Administrator maintains source-referenced MRL versions. The selected scope specifies human-mediated entry rather than direct laboratory or regulatory API integrations.')]
for title,body in components:s+='**'+title+':** '+body+'\n\n'
s+='### 1.2 Package Diagram\n\nEach UML package contains related source-code responsibilities. Dashed dependency arrows point toward the package depended upon. Frontend packages denote logical code organization without requiring a particular UI framework.\n\n'
num=1;tn=0
for j,(name,title,rows) in enumerate(packages,1):
 num+=1;tn+=1
 s+=f'#### 1.2.{j} {title}\n\n![{title}](diagrams/{name}.svg)\n\nDiagram {num}: {title}\n\n**Package Descriptions**\n\n'
 s+=table(['No','Package','Description'],[(f'{i:02}',n,d) for i,(n,d) in enumerate(rows,1)])
 s+=f'Table {tn}: {title.replace("Diagram","Descriptions")}\n\n'
s+='## 2. Database Design\n\nThe existing database diagram is supplied separately in `DBDiagram.png`, with the logical ERD in `all-in-one.svg`. This revision keeps those files unchanged and does not redraw a database diagram, as requested. Logical class names in Section 3 map through repositories to the existing physical schema.\n\n'
s+='## 3. Detailed Design\n\nClass diagrams follow the example by focusing on feature-domain objects, their typed attributes, operations and associations. Public operations describe validation, calculations or creation of new versioned records; they do not authorize editing committed ledger/evidence history. Class Specifications retain the originally requested documentation. All sequence repository calls share the coordinating application transaction where atomicity is required.\n\n'
for i,f in enumerate(manifest['features'],1):
 s+=f'### 3.{i} {f["title"]}\n\n'
 s+='Use cases: '+', '.join(f'UC-{u:02}' for u in f['ucs'])+'. '+f['overview']+'\n\n'
 s+=f'#### 3.{i}.1 Class Diagram\n\n![{f["title"]} class diagram](diagrams/{f["classdiag"]}.svg)\n\n'
 num+=1;s+=f'Diagram {num}: {f["title"]} Class Diagram\n\n**Class Specifications**\n\n'
 rows=[]
 for j,n in enumerate(groups[i-1],1):
  fields='; '.join(ty+' '+field for ty,field in selected_fields(n))
  ops='; '.join(methods.get(n,[]))
  rows.append((f'{j:02}',n,fields,ops))
 s+=table(['No','Class','Attributes','Operations'],rows);tn+=1
 s+=f'Table {tn}: {f["title"]} Class Specifications\n\n'
 s+='**Design constraints:**\n\n'+''.join('- '+x+'\n' for x in f['rules'])+'\n'
 for k,(sn,title) in enumerate(f['seqs'],2):
  s+=f'#### 3.{i}.{k} {title}\n\n![{title}](diagrams/{sn}.svg)\n\n';num+=1
  s+=f'Diagram {num}: {title} Sequence Diagram\n\n'
(ROOT/'GrainLedger_SDD.md').write_text(s)
